<html><head><meta content="text/html; charset=UTF-8" http-equiv="content-type"></head><body class="doc-content" style="background-color:#ffffff;max-width:468pt;padding:72pt 72pt 72pt 72pt"><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">NORTH LONDON &middot; EST. FOR EVAN, WHO IS OFF SOCIAL MEDIA</span></p><h1 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:24pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:24pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The Weekly Arsenal Digest</span></h1><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">EVERYTHING ARSENAL &middot; ONE CLUB, ALL FRONTS</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="font-weight:700">Wednesday, August 12, 2026</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;&middot; Pre-Season Edition</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">THE LEAD</span></h2><h1 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:24pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:24pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Champions, in name only, until Cardiff</span></h1><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">Arsenal arrive at the Principality Stadium on Sunday as Premier League champions for the first time in 22 years &mdash; and as a team that has shipped six goals in two pre-season defeats with its two best defenders in the treatment room. The Community Shield against Manchester City is a trinket. What it will reveal about Mikel Arteta&#39;s back four is anything but.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>There is a particular kind of unease that settles over a champion in August, and </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;are living in it. Eighty-three days have passed since </span><span style="font-weight:700">Mikel Arteta</span><span>&#39;s side were confirmed as Premier League champions, ending a wait that had stretched to 22 years. Seventy-four days have passed since the club watched </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Paris Saint-Germain</span><span>&nbsp;lift the European Cup in Budapest after a shootout in a final </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;did not lose in 120 minutes &mdash; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Havertz</span><span>&nbsp;inside six minutes, a </span><span style="font-weight:700">Demb&eacute;l&eacute;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;penalty on the hour, 4-3 on spot-kicks, and gone. And in the fortnight since the squad reassembled properly at London Colney, the reigning champions of England have lost two pre-season matches in a row and conceded six goals doing it.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>On Sunday afternoon in Cardiff they face </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Manchester City</span><span>&nbsp;in the </span><span style="text-decoration-skip-ink:none;-webkit-text-decoration-skip:none;color:#0000ee;text-decoration:underline"><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_FA_Community_Shield&amp;sa=D&amp;source=editors&amp;ust=1786912153255643&amp;usg=AOvVaw2HqzpY5NH7P2R78l10225p" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:inherit">FA Community Shield</a></span><span>, a fixture displaced from Wembley &mdash; booked out for concerts &mdash; to the Principality Stadium for the first time since 2006. It kicks off at 3pm British time, 7am on the West Coast, with </span><span style="font-weight:700">Sam Barrott</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;refereeing. It is, by the standards of what this squad achieved last season and expects of itself this one, a nothing game. It is also the first competitive evidence anyone will get about whether the champions have a defence.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>The problem is not conceptual, it is nominal. </span><span style="font-weight:700">William Saliba</span><span>&nbsp;is in what Arteta called &quot;rest mode&quot; &mdash; a back injury that curtailed his World Cup with </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">France</span><span>&nbsp;and which the manager described this week in terms that should worry anyone reading closely. &quot;William is in rest mode at the moment for two weeks,&quot; Arteta said. &quot;He had to do almost nothing, don&#39;t aggravate the injury. It&#39;s going to take some time to heal.&quot; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Jurri&euml;n Timber</span><span>, recovering from groin surgery in June, is &quot;still weeks away&quot; and will miss the start of the Premier League season. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Louie Copley</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">, the 18-year-old midfielder who had been one of the genuine stories of the summer, ruptured his anterior cruciate ligament ten minutes into the defeat in Dublin. That is a first-choice centre-back, a first-choice right-back and an emerging squad option, gone before a ball has been kicked in anger.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">&quot;William is in rest mode at the moment for two weeks. He had to do almost nothing, don&#39;t aggravate the injury. It&#39;s going to take some time to heal.&quot; &mdash; Mikel Arteta, on William Saliba</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>What is left is a back line assembled out of parts. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Gabriel Magalh&atilde;es</span><span>&nbsp;is fit and will partner, most likely, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Piero Hincapi&eacute;</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; whose loan from </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Bayer Leverkusen</span><span>&nbsp;was made permanent for &pound;34.5m in June and who scored the consolation against </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Real Betis</span><span>. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Cristhian Mosquera</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Ben White</span><span>, the latter only lately back to full training after two injury-bitten seasons, are the right-back options, with the 18-year-old </span><span style="font-weight:700">Theo Julienne</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; a midfielder by trade &mdash; pressed into service there through pre-season and, on the evidence of the Emirates Cup, entirely unfazed by it. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Riccardo Calafiori</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;covers the left. It is a functional group. It is not the group that won 26 league matches and conceded 27 goals across a title-winning campaign.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>The two defeats have been instructive in different ways. Against </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Real Betis</span><span>&nbsp;in Dublin on August 5, a </span><span style="font-weight:700">Kepa Arrizabalaga</span><span>&nbsp;error helped </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Betis</span><span>&nbsp;to a 2-0 lead inside the opening exchanges and </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;lost 3-1, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Rodrigo Riquelme</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Nelson Deossa</span><span>&nbsp;scoring before </span><span style="font-weight:700">Pablo Fornals</span><span>&nbsp;settled it. Arteta said his players were &quot;fuming&quot; afterwards and made clear he considered that a good sign. Four days later, in the Emirates Cup against </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Borussia Dortmund</span><span>, they were 2-0 down inside half an hour again &mdash; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Samuele Inacio</span><span>&nbsp;after seven minutes, then the 18-year-old </span><span style="font-weight:700">Konstantinos Karetsas</span><span>&nbsp;punishing a </span><span style="font-weight:700">Calafiori</span><span>&nbsp;turnover &mdash; and lost 3-2, with </span><span style="font-weight:700">Joane Gadou</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;scoring from a badly defended corner. &quot;We conceded some poor goals the other day, some poor goals today, in the way we competed,&quot; Arteta said. The shootout win afterwards was a courtesy.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>Set against that, the attacking signs are good, and they are new. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Christos Tzolis</span><span>, the &pound;34m arrival from </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Club Brugge</span><span>, has been the most consistently threatening </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;player of pre-season: a goal on debut in the 4-1 win at </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Girona</span><span>, two dangerous free-kicks and an assist for </span><span style="font-weight:700">Ethan Nwaneri</span><span>&nbsp;against </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Dortmund</span><span>, and the foul won off </span><span style="font-weight:700">Jobe Bellingham</span><span>&nbsp;that </span><span style="font-weight:700">Viktor Gy&ouml;keres</span><span>&nbsp;converted from the spot. He has started pre-season on the left wing, which is not an accident and which has consequences we address below. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Max Dowman</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">, who is 16, has a goal and an assist and looks like a footballer rather than a project.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>And then there is the midfield, which is now the most expensive </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;have ever assembled. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Bruno Guimar&atilde;es</span><span>&nbsp;signed from </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Newcastle United</span><span>&nbsp;on August 8 for &pound;75m and will wear 39. Whether he starts in Cardiff is genuinely open &mdash; he has had barely a week on the training ground &mdash; but the idea of him alongside </span><span style="font-weight:700">Declan Rice</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Mart&iacute;n Zubimendi</span><span>, with </span><span style="font-weight:700">Martin &Oslash;degaard</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Eberechi Eze</span><span>&nbsp;ahead, is the most obviously frightening thing about this </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;team. Arteta will have to choose two of three, every week, and that is a problem other managers would like to have.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">City</span><span>, for their part, arrive as FA Cup holders and as the side that finished seven points behind </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;last season with a goal difference two adrift. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Pep Guardiola</span><span>&#39;s teams have historically treated the Shield as a scrimmage and then won it anyway. The tactical question is narrow and specific: can an </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;back line without </span><span style="font-weight:700">Saliba</span><span>&nbsp;hold a high line against </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">City</span><span>&#39;s runners for ninety minutes, and if it cannot, does Arteta drop the line and concede the territory he has spent six years teaching this squad to take? On Sunday it costs nothing to find out. On August 21, against </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Coventry City</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;under the Friday-night lights at the Emirates, it starts costing points.</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Key Facts &mdash; FA Community Shield</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Fixture:</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;v </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Manchester City</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Date &amp; time:</span><span>&nbsp;Sunday, August 16 &middot; 3:00pm BST / </span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">7:00am Pacific</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Venue:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Principality Stadium, Cardiff &mdash; first Shield in Wales since 2006</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Why Cardiff:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Wembley unavailable; only the third time since 2007 the Shield has left Wembley</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Referee:</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight:700">Sam Barrott</span><span>&nbsp;(VAR: </span><span style="font-weight:700">James Bell</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700